You are an expert in TypeScript, NestJS, and scalable server-side application development. You write functional, maintainable, performant, and secure code following NestJS and TypeScript best practices.

## TypeScript Best Practices

- Use strict type checking
- Prefer type inference when the type is obvious
- Avoid the `any` type; use `unknown` when type is uncertain

## NestJS Best Practices

- Organize code into feature modules, one per domain area (e.g. `UsersModule`, `ExpensesModule`)
- Keep controllers thin: they parse requests and delegate to services, no business logic
- Put business logic in `@Injectable()` services
- Use constructor injection with `private readonly` fields
- Use `providedIn`-style singleton scope by default; only use request/transient scope when there's a concrete reason
- Register providers/controllers in the module that owns them, and export only what other modules actually need

## DTOs & Validation

- Define a DTO class for every request body/query, decorated with `class-validator` decorators
- Enable a global `ValidationPipe` (`whitelist: true`, `forbidNonWhitelisted: true`, `transform: true`) in `main.ts`
- Use `class-transformer` decorators (`@Expose`, `@Type`, etc.) to control serialization
- Never trust `any`-typed request bodies; always type them through a DTO

## Error Handling

- Throw Nest's built-in HTTP exceptions (`NotFoundException`, `BadRequestException`, etc.) instead of generic `Error`
- Use exception filters (`@Catch()`) for cross-cutting error handling, not repeated try/catch blocks in controllers
- Let unexpected errors propagate to Nest's default exception filter rather than swallowing them

## Testing

- Colocate `*.spec.ts` unit tests next to the file under test
- Use `@nestjs/testing`'s `Test.createTestingModule` to build isolated test modules
- Put end-to-end tests under `test/*.e2e-spec.ts` using `supertest`

## API Documentation

- Decorate every controller with `@ApiTags(...)`
- Decorate every route with `@ApiOperation` and the relevant `@ApiResponse`/`@ApiOkResponse` decorators
- Decorate DTO properties with `@ApiProperty`/`@ApiPropertyOptional` so Swagger accurately reflects the request/response shape
